  "final_answer": "Cause: the feed was ordered by created_at alone and the page token stored only created_at. When events shared a timestamp and a page boundary fell among them, the next page skipped the remaining tied events. Fix: the feed order is now (created_at, id), which is unique per event; the token encodes both fields (t and i); and store.page resumes strictly after that (created_at, id) position. All 7 existing tests pass. I did not add a regression test for tied timestamps, so that case is covered only by the reasoning above.",
